aufnahme for Debian/Ubuntu
==========================

A browser-based screencast recorder: record the screen, a window or a
browser tab with the microphone and an optional webcam, edit the result
with a simple cut list, export it as MP4 and publish it to filme.

Browsers only allow screen capture on HTTPS or on http://localhost, so
there are two ways to run it:

  Central server   behind a TLS reverse proxy (nginx.conf.example /
                   apache.conf.example in this directory); everyone
                   records through https://aufnahme.example.com.
  Recording PC     installed on the machine you record on; open
                   http://localhost:8073 in the browser there. Set
                   secure-cookies? #f in /etc/aufnahme/config.scm (the
                   cookies would otherwise need HTTPS) and restart. On a
                   single-user machine, auto-login-user "<name>" skips
                   the sign-in (only for http://localhost, never through
                   a proxy).

Layout
  /opt/aufnahme/app/            the app (bin, src, static)
  /opt/aufnahme/bin/scm         the dabscm runtime it was built with
  /etc/aufnahme/config.scm      the config (created on first install with a
                                fresh secret, never overwritten)
  /etc/default/aufnahme         optional: JAVA_OPTS="-Xmx512m"
  /var/lib/aufnahme/            ALL data: back up this folder
    projects/                   recordings, edits and exports
    users.scm                   users, roles and password hashes
    site/                       settings.scm (name, colours), logo, favicon
  /usr/bin/aufnahme-admin       runs a tool from app/bin (as user aufnahme)

Services
  aufnahme.service              the web app (127.0.0.1:8073 by default)
  aufnahme-health.timer         probes /healthz every minute, restarts the
                                app after two failures

First install
  1. sudo apt install ./aufnahme_<version>_all.deb
     (pulls in ffmpeg and a Java runtime; the service starts right away)
  2. Create the first administrator:
       sudo -u aufnahme aufnahme-admin user add <name> admin
  3. Central server: put the TLS reverse proxy in front.
     Recording PC: set secure-cookies? #f, then
       sudo systemctl restart aufnahme
     and open http://localhost:8073.
  4. Sign in; the start page shows what the browser can record.

Tools (run as the aufnahme user: sudo -u aufnahme aufnahme-admin <tool> ...)
  user add <name> [user|admin]  prompts for the password
  user passwd|role|disable|enable|delete <name> ...
  user list

Upgrades
  sudo apt install ./aufnahme_<newer>_all.deb restarts the services; the
  config and the data are kept. Purging the package removes /etc/aufnahme
  but keeps /var/lib/aufnahme and the system user.
